<D.RUFFER> each vocabulary does a hash scheme on the first letter of
<D.RUFFER> the name to determine which "thread" to use.
<[Kevin] APPERT> is here.
<[Kevin] APPERT> hi Jax, Dennis, Dave
<D.RUFFER> then, when you define a new vocabulary....
<D.RUFFER> you tell it the offset within the threads
<D.RUFFER> thus a word starting with a in FORTH, uses the first thread
<D.RUFFER> but the same word in EDITOR uses the second thread
<D.RUFFER> this gives a farely equal distribution to the hash tables...
<D.RUFFER> and make it very simple to follow the threads
<D.RUFFER> you understand Dave?
<[Dave] DHWEINSTEIN> Yes.
