<[Dave] DHWEINSTEIN> Well...I find it interesting that 99% of the Forth code I
write is language extensions.
<[Dave] DHWEINSTEIN> Since I have relatively little control over the C code I
write ("We need this yesterday!"), I use Forth to explore.
<[Steno] FIGCHAPTERS> The classic advice about Forth is: ....
<[Steno] FIGCHAPTERS> First you write an application-specific language in
Forth, then you write your application.
<[Dave] DHWEINSTEIN> It gives a different mindset. I.E. I've been interested
in Smalltalk style object oriented programming. So I designed some syntax, and
I'm busy writing a Forth extension for it. (Should be working in a week or
two).
<[Dave] DHWEINSTEIN> (Some of the implementation specific details are the
reason I'm hip deep in the F-PC source code)
